The modern standard for doing this is **JavaScript (React)** combined with the **Block API**. Below is a complete, step-by-step guide to creating a block named **"Hero Block"** containing a Heading, a Paragraph, and an Image.

### Prerequisites
*   **Node.js** installed on your computer.
*   **Local Environment**: It is highly recommended to use a local environment like **LocalWP**, **XAMPP**, or **Varying Vagrant Vagrants** to test custom development safely.

---

### Step 1: Create the Folder Structure
Navigate to your WordPress plugins folder (usually `/wp-content/plugins/`) and create a new folder.
**Path:** `my-custom-blocks/my-hero-block/`

Inside this folder, create a single file named `my-hero-block.php`.

### Step 2: The PHP File (Plugin Boot & Registration)
Create the following content inside `my-hero-block.php`. This registers the block and tells WordPress where the JavaScript is located.

```php
<?php
/**
 * Plugin Name: My Custom Hero Block
 * Description: A custom block with heading, text, and image.
 * Version: 1.0.0
 * Author: Your Name
 */

// Prevent direct file access
if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
    exit;
}

// Register block assets
function my_custom_block_register() {
    // Build the asset file
    $asset_file = include( plugin_dir_path( __FILE__ ) . 'build/index.asset.php' );

    // Register the block with metadata
    register_block_type( 'my-custom-blocks/hero-block', array(
        'editor_script'   => 'my-custom-block-script', // The script handle
        'script'          => false,                    // No script on frontend
        'render_callback' => 'my_custom_block_render', // The function to output HTML
    ));

    // Enqueue the script
    wp_enqueue_script(
        'my-custom-block-script',
        plugins_url( 'build/index.js', __FILE__ ),
        array( 'wp-blocks', 'wp-element', 'wp-editor' ), // Dependencies
        $asset_file['version'],
        true // Load in footer
    );
}
add_action( 'init', 'my_custom_block_register' );

// Front-end rendering function
function my_custom_block_render( $attributes ) {
    $heading = isset( $attributes['heading'] ) ? $attributes['heading'] : '';
    $content = isset( $attributes['content'] ) ? $attributes['content'] : '';
    $imageId = isset( $attributes['imageUrl'] ) ? $attributes['imageUrl'] : '';

    $imageHtml = '';
    if ( $imageId ) {
        $imageHtml = '<img src="' . esc_url( wp_get_attachment_url( $imageId ) ) . '" alt="' . esc_attr( $heading ) . '" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;" />';
    }

    return sprintf(
        '<div class="my-hero-block">
            %s
            %s
            %s
        </div>',
        '<h2 class="my-hero-heading">' . esc_html( $heading ) . '</h2>',
        '<p class="my-hero-text">' . wp_kses_post( $content ) . '</p>',
        $imageHtml
    );
}
```

